From d709dc63aa617833d27a58fb06612df38d1c0665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kadomoto <kadomoto@mtl.t.u-tokyo.ac.jp>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:40:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Accept [double] sections in smu-vp INI files

smu-vp's apply_ini_value() only handled [bool], [int], [uint] and
[string]; any other section returned without setting a preset. smc-vp's
parser already accepts [double]/[float], so an smc-vp ini that tunes a
double CCI parameter (for example dut.aou.bridge_delay_ns or
dut.clint.tick_period_ns) loaded without error in smu-vp but had no
effect. The smc_smu_vp.ini header promises identical semantics to the
smc-vp ini.

Add the [double]/[float] branch, matching smc-vp.

Add smu-aou-delay-test as a regression: its generated smc.ini sets
dut.aou.bridge_delay_ns = 10 us and dut.clint.tick_period_ns = 100 ns,
and the SMC firmware requires MTIME to advance by at least 8 hops x
bridge_delay_ns across 4 write+readback beats through the AOU. Before
this change the test fails (MTIME frozen, delay 0); after it, it passes
(~15 us/hop measured). All 9 sw/smu-vp-tests pass.
